---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Cover from '../components/Cover.astro';
import { tracks, isOpen, firstLive, lessonUrl, lessonsOf } from '../data/site';
const first = tracks.find(isOpen)!;
const start = lessonUrl(first, firstLive(first)!);
---
<Base title="learn-genai.in" description="Short lessons on working with AI for senior engineers, tech leads and engineering managers. One clear idea at a time.">
  <main>
    <section class="col hero">
      <p class="kicker">for engineers who build things</p>
      <h1 class="display">Learn to work with AI, <span class="hl">one clear idea</span> at a time.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Short lessons for senior engineers, tech leads and engineering managers. Each lesson explains one idea, shows it in a hand drawing, and ends with something you can try at work.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href={start}>Start reading</a>
        <a class="link" href={`/${first.slug}/`}>See the contents</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="wrap">
      <div class="steps">
        <div><h3>1. Read</h3><p>About five minutes. One idea, written in plain words.</p></div>
        <div><h3>2. Watch it drawn</h3><p>The idea is drawn by hand, step by step, when you scroll to it.</p></div>
        <div><h3>3. Check yourself</h3><p>One short question, so you know the idea has landed.</p></div>
        <div><h3>4. Try it at work</h3><p>One thing to do today in the tools you already use.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="col made">
      <h2 class="hand-h"><span>Not AI slop. Written by hand first.</span></h2>
      <p>Every lesson starts as my own handwritten notes. I write them while learning from papers, talks, documentation and my own work as an engineer. Then I pick what matters for people who build software, and leave out the rest.</p>
      <p>You can read the original notes for every track. AI tools help me draw the pictures, build this site and narrate the videos in my voice. I check every line before it goes out.</p>
      <a class="made-link" href="/notes/context-engineering/2026-11-15-context-engineering-notes.pdf"><img src="/notes/context-engineering/2026-11-15-page-2.jpg" alt="A page of the handwritten notes for Context engineering." width="696" height="900" loading="lazy" /><span>See the handwritten notes for Context engineering</span></a>
      <p>The same lessons, drawn and explained as short videos: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@LearnGenAIbyHand-for-you">Learn GenAI by Hand on YouTube</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="wrap book">
      <h2 class="hand-h"><span>The book so far</span></h2>
      <p>The site is written like a book, one track after another. A track opens when the notes for it are ready.</p>
      <ul class="shelf">
        {tracks.map((t) => {
          const open = isOpen(t);
          const live = lessonsOf(t).filter((l) => l.status === 'live').length;
          return (
            <li>
              {open ? (
                <a class="book-card live" href={`/${t.slug}/`}>
                  <Cover n={t.n} slug={t.slug} title={t.title} />
                  <span class="book-meta"><span class="book-title">{t.title}</span><span class="book-blurb">{t.blurb}</span><span class="book-tag open">Open now · {live} of {lessonsOf(t).length} lessons</span></span>
                </a>
              ) : (
                <div class="book-card planned" aria-disabled="true">
                  <Cover n={t.n} slug={t.slug} title={t.title} />
                  <span class="book-meta"><span class="book-title">{t.title}</span><span class="book-blurb">{t.blurb}</span><span class="book-tag">{t.label ?? 'Coming'}</span></span>
                </div>
              )}
            </li>
          );
        })}
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
